  "text_pages": [
    "ERASMUS+ Timeline\nERASMUS+ Timeline\nBefore arrival\nAfter arrival\nBefore departure\nBefore arrival\nSPRING / AUTUMN\nyou are nominated by your home university coordinator - an email sent to\nekotouc@rek.zcu.cz\nbefore the following deadlines:\n1st May\n(20th April for visa students) for winter semester\n15th November\n(20th October for visa students) for summer semester\nMAY/OCTOBER\nyou fill in the\nonline registration\non UWB Portal (faculty coordinator is assigned to you, choice of courses) + accommodation application (by email to\nekotouc@rek.zcu.cz\n)\nMAY / OCTOBER\nVisa application (visa students only!) - you will receive Letter of Acceptance and Proof of Accommodation (after having paid the reservation fee of 6 000,-CZK) by post (you will submit those documents to the embassy)\nJUNE / NOVEMBER\nyou create your Learning Agreement (the document is generated on Portal within your online registration or via EWP) and you send it to the faculty coordinator\nlate JUNE / DECEMBER\nErasmus coordinator informs the students by email about their assigned place at the dorms + the instructions how to pay the reservation fee 6 000,-CZK\nAUGUST / JANUARY\nJIS card e-application, Buddy application, ORION account activation\nSEPTEMBER / FEBRUARY\nyou will arrive at the UWB when new semester begins\nBack\nAfter arrival\nSEPTEMBER / FEBRUARY\nyou will check-in at the reception of the university dormitory  + you will sign the Accommodation contract with the head of the dormitory and  make necessary payment (rent)\nSEPTEMBER / FEBRUARY\nyou will come to say Hello to the International Office coordinator where you will be officially welcomed and accepted - if needed, you will receive the Certificate of Arrival at the International Office\nSEPTEMBER / FEBRUARY\nyou go to collect your JIS card at HelpDesk office (street Univerzitní 20, Bory campus)\nSEPTEMBER / FEBRUARY\nyou can participate in the Orientation Week which is organized by ESN UWB Pilsen one week before the semester starts\nAUTUMN / SPRING\nyou attend the lectures and seminars.\nYou can make the changes in your study plan and submit Changes of Learning agreement (CHLA) to your faculty coordinator if necessary (you have around 1 month to do it).\nJANUARY / JUNE\nafter the lectures finish, you take the exams\nBack\nBefore departure\nFEBRUARY / JUNE\nyou will get Transcript of Records (the results of the courses which you studied) from your faculty coordinator\nFEBRUARY / JUNE\nyou will get Certificate of Attendance at the International Office\nFEBRUARY / JUNE\nyou do not forget to come to say good bye to the International Office ;o)\nFinally you leave Pilsen\nBack"
  ],
